Showtime 48.1 on Python 3.9: OpenIndiana's PyGObject (library/python/pygobject-39)
exists only for Python 3.9, and Showtime uses Python 3.10 syntax.

- "match" statements become if/elif/else on the same values (all patterns are
  literals, dotted constants or the "_" wildcard).
- Modules with "X | None" annotations get "from __future__ import annotations",
  so the annotations are not evaluated.

Not for upstream (Showtime requires Python >= 3.10); drop it once
OpenIndiana ships PyGObject for a newer Python.
Upstream: https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/showtime

